Design for Quality-testing is a testing control of the product recovered. Many techniques can be performed in order to determine if the product is still qualitative acceptable, but this is dipends to the product under consideration. Some tests involve visual inspections testing and/or functional testing. Different testing can help to evaluate different factors, such as aesthetic, functional, mechanical, and software factors. The complexity of this strategy tends to increase for decrising volumes. 

In desining for quality-testing it is important to take in consideration:
- Determining the feasibility of the recovery process.
- Verification of the backup facilities.
- Ensuring proper steps are documented to verify the compatibility of backup facilities.
- Providing Training within the team.
- Demonstrating the ability of the organization to recover from all critical failures.
- Maintaining and updating the recovery plan at regular intervals.